3. Identify the `r` largest elements in the sorted array. These are `a[n-r], a[n-r+1], ..., a[n-1]` (using 0-based indexing).
4. The median of this subarray (which is already sorted) is the element at the `p`-th position, where `p = (r + 1) / 2` (1-based index within the subarray).
5. The index of this median element in the original sorted array `a` (0-based) is `(n - r) + p - 1`.

